My favorite starting strategy involves playing a Valkyrie.
I have described it here long ago, but I'll do it again for
the new players.  Also, since I quit reading this newsgroup
for a while I'm not sure that all of the tricks for PL6 still
work in PL7.



Play a Valkyrie so that you start out with a good long sword.
Quickly go to level 3, leaving a trail of blood along the way.
At dlevel 3 you can easily get to experience level 5, at
which time you can go to a fountain and #dip your sword.
Sooner or later a hand will bless the sword and you are ready
for lots of action.  (This character doesn't need to kick
monsters.  His sword will take care of them.)

Disclamer:  I'm not responsible if something jumps out of
the fountain and kills you!

Also, when it's time to pray get yourself down to <5 hit points
and pray.  You usually gain extra points this way.  You can reduce
your hit points by

	1. standing on a stairway and by letting a monster bite you
	2. kicking a wall
	3. throwing your sword upwards so it falls on your head
	4. combining all of the above

With this plan (and a little practice) you can easily get to dlevel
15 or lower.  To get much lower than this it usually takes magic!

Another plan of mine:  Don't upset the shopkeepers.  I know it's
fun to steal, but it can be advantageous for several reasons to
be on good terms with the shopkeepers.
For instance:

	1. you can use them to determine the worth of gems
	2. you can use them to keep monsters away from you
	   while you regenerate.  (Pick up an item in the shop
	   and the keeper will block the door.)
	3. if you have a ring of conflict, the shopkeeper will
	   kill all sorts of nasty monsters for you.
	4. they'll kill you with little reason

Usually, after my character gets to be pretty tough, I'll go
back and kill the shopkeeper to retrieve all the money I spent
in his shop.

